PROBLEM STATEMENT

Write a program to demonstrate list and related functions in Python.
ALGORITHM:

STEP 1 : Start the program.
STEP 2 : Create a list with some elements.
STEP 3 : Display the original list.
STEP 4 : Add a new element to the list using the append() function.
STEP 5 : Insert an element at a specific position using the insert() function.
STEP 6 : Remove an element from the list using the remove() function.
STEP 7 : Display the length of the list using the len() function.
STEP 8 : Sort the elements of the list using the sort() function.
STEP 9 : Print all results using the print() function.
STEP 10 : Stop the program.
lst = [10, 20, 30, 40]

print("\nOriginal List:")
print(lst)

lst.append(50)
print("\nAfter append:")
print(lst)

lst.insert(2, 25)
print("\nAfter insert:")
print(lst)

lst.remove(30)
print("\nAfter remove:")
print(lst)

print("\nLength of List:")
print(len(lst))

lst.sort()
print("\nSorted List:")
print(lst)
